  "claim_boundary": "Ports are typed addresses over source-authored GLB node names. The generated runtime derivative adds one deterministic view clip over the three named BAND nodes while CORE remains fixed. The 3+1 deck reads the declared transform contract analytically and compares local frames; its pairwise phase portrait is the 1:1 ellipse implied by the declared 120-degree offsets. The Orientation Ledger treats PIN as a fixed relation origin and H/X plus V/Y as pair-coordinate references; it measures angle, radius, sector, axis relations, crossings and winding without creating new GLB geometry. The red seam is a current display difference vector, not a fourth band, GLB node or algorithm binding. The deck is not a material measurement and does not add a clock. Neither layer modifies a source GLB or establishes a native breathing process, causal operator, semantic truth, material behavior or physical coupling. The dense model remains one unsegmented geometry mesh."
